\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 1. \'93I had three apps for one workflow\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Hook:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93I had three apps open just to think through one idea.\'94\

\f0\b Talk track:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93I was writing notes in one app, sketching flows in another, and tracking little tasks somewhere else. And every time I switched tools, I lost the thread. So I built DevBoard to keep the whole workflow in one place: notes, canvas, links, files, all together.\'94\

\f0\b Show:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Quick split-screen: Obsidian-style notes, Miro-style board, Notion-style table \u8594  DevBoard canvas.\

\f0\b CTA:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93It\'92s free, no account, and your files stay yours.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 2. \'93For people who almost like Notion\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Hook:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93I love the idea of Notion. I just don\'92t always want\'85 Notion.\'94\

\f0\b Talk track:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93Sometimes I don\'92t need a full productivity operating system. I just want a folder where I can write notes, connect ideas, and sketch things out without setting up a whole workspace. That\'92s what DevBoard is for.\'94\

\f0\b Show:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 You on camera first, then screen recording of opening a folder and making a quick note.\

\f0\b CTA:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93Try it if you want notes that feel lighter.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 3. \'93The notes app that is literally a folder\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Hook:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93This notes app is basically just a folder on your computer.\'94\

\f0\b Talk track:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93You pick a folder. DevBoard turns it into a workspace. Your notes are still plain files. You can open them in another editor, back them up, sync them however you want, or just keep them local.\'94\

\f0\b Show:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Open DevBoard \u8594  show notes \u8594  open same folder in Finder/Explorer \u8594  open a file in TextEdit/Notepad.\

\f0\b CTA:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93No lock-in. No weird export process.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 4. \'93Second brain, but normal\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Hook:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93I wanted a second brain app for people who don\'92t say \'91second brain.\'92\'94\

\f0\b Talk track:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93I just wanted my notes to connect to each other. Like, if I\'92m writing about a project and mention another note, I can link it and jump there later. That\'92s it. Useful, simple, no three-hour tutorial.\'94\

\f0\b Show:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Type 
\f2\fs26 [[
\f1\fs24  or start linking one note to another.\

\f0\b CTA:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93DevBoard is for notes that quietly connect.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 5. \'93The chaotic desktop problem\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Hook:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93My writing process used to be: \'91final draft,\'92 \'91final final draft,\'92 \'91actually final draft,\'92 and \'91please use this one.\'92\'94\

\f0\b Talk track:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93I wanted one place for drafts, references, scene ideas, character notes, and the messy whiteboard part of writing. DevBoard lets me keep the chaos, but make it usable.\'94\

\f0\b Show:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Cluttered desktop visual \u8594  DevBoard workspace with folders/notes/canvas.\

\f0\b CTA:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93Especially useful if your brain works in piles.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 6. \'93Not a productivity cult\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Hook:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93I don\'92t want to join a productivity cult. I just want to remember my ideas.\'94\

\f0\b Talk track:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93A lot of apps make you feel like you need a system before you can start. DevBoard is more like: open a folder, write the thing, link the related thing, move on.\'94\

\f0\b Show:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Simple screen recording: open folder, write note, drag sticky on canvas.\

\f0\b CTA:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93No setup ritual required.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 7. \'93Why I built it\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Hook:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93I built DevBoard because I kept losing ideas between tools.\'94\

\f0\b Talk track:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93I\'92d have notes in one place, diagrams somewhere else, references in another app, and little tasks scattered everywhere. DevBoard is my attempt to make a workspace that feels like a desk: notes here, board there, files right next to them.\'94\

\f0\b Show:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 Talking head \u8594  cut to DevBoard with a note, canvas, and file sidebar.\

\f0\b CTA:
\f1\b0 \uc0\u8232 \'93It\'92s still early, but it\'92s already useful.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

